* Add a Lua rule format in which rules are Lua scripts returning a rule
  table, with the usual helper methods available as Lua globals.
* Add a Lua configuration file format, considered when no YAML
  configuration file is found.
* Add the `-e`/`--engine` option to select the rule engine to use:
  `yaml` (default, deprecated) or `lua`.
* Ship every official rule in both formats, alongside the
  `scripts/yaml2lua.py` converter.

See the full changelog of this release at
https://gitlab.com/islandoftex/arara/-/blob/development/CHANGELOG.md
